# FINMENTOR response headers
#
# STATUS: INERT ON THE CURRENT HOST.
#
# This file uses the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` convention. The site is served
# by GitHub Pages (verified live: `Server: GitHub.com`, Fastly edge), which does NOT read
# this file and does not allow custom response headers by any other means either. Nothing
# below is applied to production today.
#
# It is kept, and completed, so that the correct policy is already in place the moment the
# site is fronted by an edge layer that honours it. Do not treat its presence as evidence
# that these headers are live — verify with a real request:
#
#   curl -sI https://www.finmentor.md/ | grep -i -E 'content-security|strict-transport|x-frame|referrer|x-content-type|permissions'
#
# See docs/FINMENTOR_SECURITY_HEADERS_PLATFORM_BLOCKER.md for the migration options.
#
# Of the six headers the audit found missing, exactly one has a browser-honoured HTML
# equivalent that works on GitHub Pages today: Referrer-Policy, applied as
# <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"> on every page.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://ghennadi.app.n8n.cloud; upgrade-insecure-requests

/
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

/index.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

/*.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
